## INT-002d — Verification + operator runbook

### Test pyramid

| Level | File | Requires DB |
| ----- | ---- | ----------- |
| L0 | `test/tour-published-rollout-closure.contract.spec.ts` | no |
| L1 | existing unit specs (payload, dispatch payload) | no |
| L2 | `test/4-integration/tour-published-outbox.spec.ts` | yes |
| L3 | same file (`second dispatch → 0`, single job row) | yes |

**L2 flow:**

```text
denali tenant + integration connection (seedDefaultEventPolicies → TourPublished)
→ runPreTransactionValidation (golden publish-ready + catalogRefAllowlists)
→ persistTourUpdateAtomically (draft → active)
→ assert outbox eventType TourPublished, schemaVersion 1, deliverySnapshot.title
```

**L3 flow:**

```text
→ dispatchIntegrationDomainEvent(row) → enqueued count 1
→ replay same domainEventId → enqueued count 0 (idempotent skip)
→ assert integration_delivery_jobs row count 1, status pending
```

**L0 contract asserts:**

- This plan doc exists
- Policy migration glob exists
- Runbook exists
- Web fallback not `TourCreated` for telegram
- Drift detector symbol wired

### Runbook

`docs/dev/runbooks/tour-published-telegram-delivery.mdoc`

Sections: preconditions, env flags, deploy order, smoke SQL/queries, failure matrix, republish semantics, rollback notes.

Cross-link from [integration-event-catalog](./integration-event-catalog.mdoc).

### i18n (web)

Add `settings.integrations.eventNames.TourPublished` and `eventHints.TourPublished` in message bundles.

---

## Deploy order (mandatory)

```text
1. Merge INT-002a → deploy API + web (catalog clarity)
2. pnpm --filter @app-tour/workspace-denali build
3. Merge INT-002b → pnpm --filter @apps/api run db:migrate:deploy
4. Verify drift report = 0 (or run CLI repair)
5. Merge INT-002c → run remap --dry-run → --apply
6. Set env (staging/prod):
     OUTBOX_RELAY_ENABLED=true
     INTEGRATION_DELIVERY_ENABLED=true
     INTEGRATION_DELIVERY_WORKER_ENABLED=true
7. Restart API + worker processes
8. Runbook smoke: publish tour → Telegram channel
9. Optional: TOUR_PUBLISHED_ROLLOUT_GATE_FATAL=true on staging
```

**Failure mode if order violated:** steps 3–4 skipped while domain emit active → publish works, Telegram silent. Drift detector + runbook exist to catch this.

---

## Republish semantics (documented — no code suppress)

Each `draft → active` transition emits new `TourPublished:{tourId}:{rowVersion}` → new delivery job. Relay replay of same `domainEventId` is idempotent via `uq_integration_delivery_jobs_idempotency`.

Product choice: **notify on every publish transition** (Stripe-style). Not suppressed in INT-002.

---

## Rollback

| Layer | Strategy |
| ----- | -------- |
| SQL migration | Forward-only; do not DELETE TourPublished rows in rollback |
| Emergency | Architect-approved hotfix only: temporarily re-add surface `TourCreated` mapping (ADR amend required) |
| Normal | Fix forward: run policy backfill + intent remap |

